1
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:07,380
Are you looking at naked tribeswomen?

2
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:10,000
No, look.

3
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:12,340
That's a pig.

4
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,340
I know. But look at the knobs on it!

5
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,890
Hey.

6
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,890
Hey.

7
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:23,060
Emily's cousin kicked me out.

8
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:24,520
What?

9
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:24,520
Why?

10
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:27,350
When you sublet from your wife's cousin...

11
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:31,820
...then you divorce, sometimes the cousin wants his apartment back.

12
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:33,530
Didn't you sign a lease?

13
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,200
Who needs a lease when it's "family"?

14
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:40,700
You can stay with us.

15
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,330
Anything you need.

16
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:45,410
But you have to let us know when you feel better...

17
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:47,420
...so we can make fun of your hair.

18
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,300
You got it.

19
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,300
Okay.

20
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:56,220
Thanks, I really appreciate this. I'm going to get packing again.

21
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:59,930
I've been moving around so much that I feel like a nomad.

22
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:05,100
What?

23
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:05,100
He thought you said gonad.

24
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:02,570
Wow, Monica. If every place were this clean, it'd be tough making a living.

25
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,660
Ha, oh, Larry!

26
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:07,750
Um, do health inspectors work on commission?

27
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,370
No, bribes.

28
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:12,670
Ha-ha-ha, it's okay to laugh?

29
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:12,670
I was just kidding.

30
00:02:14,090 --> 00:02:16,840
I'll check the kitchen floor.

31
00:02:14,090 --> 00:02:16,840
Knock yourself out.

32
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:20,380
Yummy! Heh.

33
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:22,510
Larry?

34
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:24,560
Yeah, I'd let him check out my kitchen floor.

35
00:02:29,270 --> 00:02:30,440
A 98.

36
00:02:31,230 --> 00:02:33,480
I deducted two points for not wearing your hat.

37
00:02:33,650 --> 00:02:35,520
That is a Section 5 violation.

38
00:02:35,690 --> 00:02:38,690
Oh. Now look, Larry, honey, ha, ha.

39
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:41,570
Um, I wrote the book on Section 5.

40
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:44,370
You only need to wear it in the kitchen.

41
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:47,240
Where's your hat?

42
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:47,240
In the kitchen. I'll get it.

43
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:50,080
Ah, there's the two points!

44
00:02:51,790 --> 00:02:54,590
You should really read that book you wrote.

45
00:03:00,510 --> 00:03:01,630
Wow.

46
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:06,850
You saw the hat in the kitchen and knew she'd go in hatless to get it, heh.

47
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:10,480
You could have your own health inspector detective show.

48
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:13,020
Ah, I don't know about that.

49
00:03:13,230 --> 00:03:15,900
But then I could be your sidekick, Voonda, heh.

50
00:03:16,690 --> 00:03:20,110
Maybe, uh, I could ask Voonda to dinner sometime?

51
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:22,360
She would love that...

52
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:25,820
...since you know all the clean places to eat, heh.

53
00:03:27,370 --> 00:03:28,410
I'll call you.

54
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:30,200
Okay.

55
00:03:34,670 --> 00:03:36,630
He's so funny! Whoa, oh.

56
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:45,010
Thank you.

57
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:45,010
Thanks.

58
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:48,890
How's Ross doing since all the Emily stuff?

59
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:51,560
He's not great. But, um, he's dealing with it.

60
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:53,230
Oh.

61
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:53,230
Wait, you're not...

62
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:57,360
Oh, I can't get started with all that Ross stuff again.

63
00:03:57,610 --> 00:04:00,150
He'll be screwed up for a long time.

64
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:04,070
Besides, I don't go for guys right after they get divorced.

65
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:07,700
Right, you only go for them five minutes before they get married.

66
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:15,710
Two pounds of mocha java.

67
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:15,710
It's Danny.

68
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,330
Are you going to go out again?

69
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:20,300
I don't know. He hasn't called since we went out.

70
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:22,590
I see him in the hallway. We flirt. I'm all...

71
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,430
...and then nothing.

72
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:28,850
Hey.

73
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:28,850
Hi, Danny.

74
00:04:29,010 --> 00:04:30,310
Wow, thirsty, huh?

75
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:34,020
I'm having a party on Saturday. Sort of a housewarming thing.

76
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:35,730
Oh, fun.

77
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:35,730
Oh, great!

78
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:37,730
Really looking forward to it.

79
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:37,730
Yeah.

80
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,440
See you!

81
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:46,820
So I guess we won't be warming his house.

82
00:04:46,990 --> 00:04:49,160
Oh, ha, ha, okay.

83
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:51,870
All right, I see what he's doing.

84
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:56,160
He's not asking me out because he wants me to ask him out.

85
00:04:56,370 --> 00:04:57,500
And you won't do that.

86
00:04:57,710 --> 00:04:59,080
That's right!

87
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:02,380
Because that would give him the control.

88
00:05:02,630 --> 00:05:05,760
So now he comes up with this "I've got a party" thing...

89
00:05:06,010 --> 00:05:08,640
...to get me to hint for an invitation.

90
00:05:08,890 --> 00:05:10,760
Blew up in his face, didn't it? Ha.

91
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,890
So there is no party?

92
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:17,940
No, there's a party. There's a party.

93
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:19,650
But the power?

94
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:22,020
That is still up for grabs.

95
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,230
You follow me?

96
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:25,740
I think so.

97
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:29,870
So he won't invite you to his party because he likes you?

98
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:31,280
Exactly!

99
00:05:40,670 --> 00:05:42,090
Ross?

100
00:05:42,630 --> 00:05:45,130
Hey, roomies!

101
00:05:46,510 --> 00:05:48,090
I love what you've done with the place.

102
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:50,680
Oh, I know it's a lot of boxes.

103
00:05:50,890 --> 00:05:54,850
I appreciate you letting me stay here.

104
00:05:50,890 --> 00:05:54,850
Not a problem.

105
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:57,140
Since you'll be here a while...

106
00:05:57,350 --> 00:06:00,350
...we, uh, could put your name on the answering machine.

107
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:02,480
Oh, I, uh, hope you don't mind...

108
00:06:02,690 --> 00:06:06,070
...but I kind of already jazzed it up a little, ha, ha.

109
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:08,150
Check it out.

110
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:18,330
We will We will call you back

111
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:22,210
Pretty cool, huh?

112
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:22,210
Oh, yes.

113
00:06:25,210 --> 00:06:27,380
You're fake laughing too, right?

114
00:06:25,210 --> 00:06:27,380
The tears are real.

115
00:06:27,550 --> 00:06:28,760
Oh, yeah. Ha, ha.

116
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:34,510
You look beautiful this evening.

117
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:34,510
Heh.

118
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:36,680
Show me the badge again.

119
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,360
Shiny, ha, ha.

120
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:48,610
Oh, you mind if I wash up? Who knows where these have been?

121
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:50,950
You are just nonstop, ha-ha-ha!

122
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:03,580
We're out of here.

123
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:03,580
Why?

124
00:07:03,790 --> 00:07:07,670
I saw ten violations. I'm shutting this place down!

125
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:11,510
You have the power to do that?

126
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:11,510
This does.

127
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,090
Shut it down.

128
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:26,900
Hey.

129
00:07:28,730 --> 00:07:29,860
What are you doing?

130
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:32,030
Nothing.

131
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:35,200
You built a fort, didn't you?

132
00:07:37,910 --> 00:07:39,410
Kind of, heh.

133
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:43,170
Oh, my God! The air purifier. Ross' air purifier.

134
00:07:43,370 --> 00:07:45,380
All I heard for four years through college was...

135
00:07:48,750 --> 00:07:50,760
You should have gone out once in a while.

136
00:07:51,590 --> 00:07:54,180
I hate this thing!

137
00:07:51,590 --> 00:07:54,180
Come on, Chandler.

138
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:57,010
Ross is our friend. He needs us right now.

139
00:07:57,260 --> 00:08:00,470
So why don't you be a grownup and come watch TV in the fort?

140
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,900
Oh, hi, Danny.

141
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,900
Hey, guys.

142
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,820
Uh, I wanted to invite you to the party.

143
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:12,070
Oh, thanks, I'll try to stop by.

144
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:15,860
Actually, I think, ahem, I'm going to be busy.

145
00:08:16,070 --> 00:08:17,280
You are?

146
00:08:17,450 --> 00:08:18,660
Yeah.

147
00:08:18,830 --> 00:08:21,160
Remember? I've got that, uh, gala.

148
00:08:23,290 --> 00:08:24,620
What's the gala for?

149
00:08:24,790 --> 00:08:26,250
Uh, it's a, um...

150
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:28,710
It's, uh, a regatta gala.

151
00:08:29,380 --> 00:08:30,670
Do you sail?

152
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:33,720
No, but I support it.

153
00:08:34,970 --> 00:08:37,970
I hope I see you tomorrow night. Take care.

154
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:39,850
Okay.

155
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:45,190
Walked right into that one, didn't he?

156
00:08:45,390 --> 00:08:46,650
What one?

157
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:49,560
You wanted him to invite you and he did.

158
00:08:49,770 --> 00:08:52,860
He waited until the last minute. So if I said yes...

159
00:08:53,070 --> 00:08:56,860
...he'd know I had nothing better to do than wait for his invitation.

160
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:58,410
But I said no...

161
00:08:58,620 --> 00:09:01,450
...which puts me back in the driver's seat.

162
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:04,080
So the ball is in his court?

163
00:09:04,290 --> 00:09:05,370
Ball?

164
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,460
No, there's no ball.

165
00:09:18,550 --> 00:09:19,840
Joey, please.

166
00:09:20,050 --> 00:09:21,810
Sorry.

167
00:09:38,410 --> 00:09:40,320
Hello, children.

168
00:09:38,410 --> 00:09:40,320
Hey.

169
00:09:40,490 --> 00:09:43,410
You want to play some foosball? Please?

170
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:46,200
Okay.

171
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:46,200
No, no, no.

172
00:09:46,410 --> 00:09:50,250
We moved the table into my room because of all the boxes, ha, ha.

173
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:52,130
Come on!

174
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,630
I have one question.

175
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:02,720
What is the deal with this?

176
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:06,600
Bye-bye, little puppet Joey hand?

177
00:10:06,810 --> 00:10:08,890
No, the quiet down thing.

178
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:11,440
Oh. You mean this.

179
00:10:11,650 --> 00:10:13,400
Mm-hm.

180
00:10:14,690 --> 00:10:17,030
I don't know how much more I can take.

181
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:21,320
Did you know he taped over my Baywatch tape with a show about bugs?

182
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:24,620
My God!

183
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,160
What if that had been porn?

184
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,160
Oh!

185
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:30,080
All right, this may be tough...

186
00:10:30,290 --> 00:10:32,880
...but it's Ross. I survived college with him.

187
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:36,340
I guess I can hold out a little longer.

188
00:10:36,550 --> 00:10:38,720
Let's have a game.

189
00:10:36,550 --> 00:10:38,720
Okay.

190
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:41,380
Don't be scored on. No, no, no.

191
00:10:41,550 --> 00:10:44,800
Yes. Ha-ha-ha.

192
00:10:44,970 --> 00:10:46,010
Uh, fellas?

193
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,480
So he's out of here.

194
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,480
Mm-hm.

195
00:11:00,450 --> 00:11:01,860
Hey.

196
00:11:00,450 --> 00:11:01,860
Hey.

197
00:11:02,030 --> 00:11:06,120
Got anything to eat? I went to Jono's and it was closed.

198
00:11:06,330 --> 00:11:10,870
Oh, I took Larry there, but it was all violated, so we shut it down.

199
00:11:11,710 --> 00:11:15,840
If this guy keeps closing our favorite places, where will we eat?

200
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:17,750
I don't know. Clean places?

201
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,300
Mm, yum!

202
00:11:25,220 --> 00:11:26,260
It's Danny.

203
00:11:26,430 --> 00:11:28,770
Don't let him in! I'm supposed to be at a gala.

204
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:32,310
We'll be right there. Can't you say it's later?

205
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:36,110
What kind of a regatta gala starts at night?

206
00:11:36,610 --> 00:11:37,900
The fake kind.

207
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:45,740
Um, I need a ladle. You got a ladle?

208
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:45,740
We have a ladle.

209
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:49,080
See you at the party.

210
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:50,290
Okay, great.

211
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:54,920
You know what Larry would say? He'd say, "See you ladle."

212
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:03,760
I'm done. You want anything? Uh, sports? International?

213
00:12:03,970 --> 00:12:05,220
Apartment listings?

214
00:12:05,970 --> 00:12:07,050
I'll take sports.

215
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,600
Mine!

216
00:12:10,310 --> 00:12:11,890
All right, uh, international.

217
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,140
That's mine too.

218
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:16,860
I'm Italian.

219
00:12:18,230 --> 00:12:22,820
I could check apartment listings, though there's never anything here.

220
00:12:23,030 --> 00:12:25,490
Not even on page seven?

221
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:27,990
Oh, yeah.

222
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:30,910
You're right. Oh, here's an affordable place.

223
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:35,460
Two bedroom, close to work. Ooh, it's available in five weeks.

224
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:37,710
What about that circled one?

225
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:42,340
Ooh, I don't know. It's kind of expensive for a studio.

226
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:44,260
But it's available now.

227
00:12:44,470 --> 00:12:45,510
Isn't it?

228
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:47,340
Yes, it is.

229
00:12:47,550 --> 00:12:49,430
Let's go look at it, heh!

230
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:52,930
Oh, okay. Let's go.

231
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:52,930
There we go! Yay!

232
00:12:53,810 --> 00:13:00,270
Oh, oh, oh, guys, would you, uh, chip in for some new air filters for the purifier?

233
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:03,490
I mean, after all, we are all using it.

234
00:13:03,650 --> 00:13:04,740
Let's go quicker!

235
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:06,320
Yeah.

236
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,290
Oh, my God!

237
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,290
Mm.

238
00:13:20,590 --> 00:13:24,590
Oh, look at this kitchen/bathroom.

239
00:13:25,050 --> 00:13:27,760
That's great! So you can cook while in the tub.

240
00:13:28,550 --> 00:13:30,470
Somebody was using his head.

241
00:13:32,310 --> 00:13:34,140
Let's check out the rest of the place.

242
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:46,320
I think this is it.

243
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:49,910
I don't know. Maybe we should keep looking.

244
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:52,700
But this place is available now.

245
00:13:52,910 --> 00:13:55,950
You don't want to be stuck with us for five weeks.

246
00:14:02,210 --> 00:14:04,500
So you think I should take this place?

247
00:14:04,670 --> 00:14:07,380
Oh, it's perfect!

248
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:12,550
How about you?

249
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:15,310
Kitchen, slash, bathroom.

250
00:14:18,270 --> 00:14:20,140
Ah, I see what you guys are saying.

251
00:14:20,310 --> 00:14:24,020
I'll, uh, go downstairs and fill out an application.

252
00:14:28,490 --> 00:14:30,610
We are bad people.

253
00:14:31,450 --> 00:14:34,950
He knew we were trying to get rid of him.

254
00:14:37,250 --> 00:14:39,120
Could we get a bathtub in our kitchen?

255
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:45,710
Ready for dinner?

256
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:47,920
Ooh, absolutely.

257
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:47,920
Great.

258
00:14:48,130 --> 00:14:50,380
You wanted to go to the Italian place on Bleecker St?

259
00:14:50,550 --> 00:14:52,260
Oh, I love that place, ha, ha.

260
00:14:52,510 --> 00:14:54,600
So no.

261
00:14:52,510 --> 00:14:54,600
Oh.

262
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:56,510
How about Mama Lozetti's?

263
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,890
Yuck.

264
00:14:58,060 --> 00:14:59,850
Sure.

265
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:03,310
How long has that milk been sitting out?

266
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:06,150
No, this place is totally healthy.

267
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,940
This milk is mine. I bought this today...

268
00:15:09,150 --> 00:15:12,280
...because I was thirsty for milk, you know?

269
00:15:16,370 --> 00:15:18,490
Okay, let's go.

270
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:22,290
Hey, buddy.

271
00:15:22,580 --> 00:15:27,670
Health Code 11 B requires that refuse be taken out the back exit.

272
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:30,170
But then I have to go all the way around.

273
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:33,090
So you choose convenience over health?

274
00:15:33,590 --> 00:15:35,850
Stop, Larry.

275
00:15:36,010 --> 00:15:41,600
Can't you just be Larry and not Larry the health inspector guy?

276
00:15:41,810 --> 00:15:43,690
It was exciting at first.

277
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:48,400
But now, it's like, so where are we going to eat ever?

278
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:52,320
I suppose I could give him a warning.

279
00:15:52,490 --> 00:15:54,160
Thank you.

280
00:15:54,950 --> 00:15:57,410
Go, go!

281
00:15:59,910 --> 00:16:03,580
If, after dinner, you still need to bust someone...

282
00:16:03,790 --> 00:16:05,710
...I know a hot dog vendor who picks his nose.

283
00:16:11,050 --> 00:16:14,880
Maybe we did good, helping Ross get back on his feet.

284
00:16:15,090 --> 00:16:16,720
That was a nice place.

285
00:16:16,930 --> 00:16:22,180
No closet space, but he could hang his stuff out the window in a bag.

286
00:16:26,270 --> 00:16:27,360
What do we do?

287
00:16:27,860 --> 00:16:29,400
I don't know.

288
00:16:29,610 --> 00:16:31,320
Maybe pizza?

289
00:16:32,650 --> 00:16:34,450
About Ross!

290
00:16:32,650 --> 00:16:34,450
Oh.

291
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,950
Hello.

292
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,540
Oh, yeah.

293
00:16:43,710 --> 00:16:47,420
It's the apartment manager. Ross put us as references.

294
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:50,840
Ross is the greatest guy. He's very reliable...

295
00:16:51,090 --> 00:16:55,510
Of course, he has a big, huge dog that, uh, barks into the night.

296
00:16:57,430 --> 00:16:59,890
Well, who doesn't love dogs?

297
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,930
Uh, he's a tap dancer.

298
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:06,850
Yes, some would say that is a lost art.

299
00:17:07,650 --> 00:17:08,690
He's a pimp!

300
00:17:10,730 --> 00:17:12,860
There you go. He's a pimp.

301
00:17:13,110 --> 00:17:15,150
He's a big, tap-dancing pimp!

302
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:18,530
Hello?

303
00:17:29,330 --> 00:17:30,500
Oh.

304
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:41,010
Watching for a sound To lead me to wherever...

305
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:44,310
Shh, this is never going to work. He's right there.

306
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,680
Just go say hi.

307
00:17:45,850 --> 00:17:51,480
I have to go downstairs and back up, as if I'm coming home from the gala.

308
00:17:51,650 --> 00:17:55,110
So just go distract him. But don't be sexy.

309
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,070
Hey, Danny.

310
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,070
Hey.

311
00:17:58,240 --> 00:17:59,280
What's going on?

312
00:17:59,530 --> 00:18:02,830
This is a great party. Great food, ha, ha.

313
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:07,790
Oh, you know, most parties, it's, uh, all chips and salsa, chips and salsa.

314
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:11,080
So, um...

315
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,840
What's this?

316
00:18:14,710 --> 00:18:15,760
Salad.

317
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,510
Oh.

318
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:20,090
And what's this?

319
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:22,930
Bread.

320
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:24,850
Aren't you a chef?

321
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:27,640
Oh.

322
00:18:27,810 --> 00:18:30,020
Hey, Rachel.

323
00:18:27,810 --> 00:18:30,020
Hey.

324
00:18:30,190 --> 00:18:33,190
Oh, right, tonight was your party.

325
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,530
You look great! I'm glad you made it.

326
00:18:35,730 --> 00:18:39,490
Oh, well, you know, the gala had to end sometime.

327
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,570
Don't go anywhere. I'll be right back.

328
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:43,990
Yeah, sure.

329
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:43,990
All right?

330
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:47,700
Whose court is the ball in now?

331
00:18:48,290 --> 00:18:49,910
I thought there wasn't a ball.

332
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:56,340
Come on. He's glad I came. He doesn't want me to go anywhere.

333
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:58,460
Ball's flying all over the place.

334
00:19:00,050 --> 00:19:01,680
This is my friend, Tom.

335
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:04,510
This is the girl I told you about.

336
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:07,930
Oh, come on! You telling people about me?

337
00:19:08,140 --> 00:19:10,640
I think you two could really hit it off.

338
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,850
I'm gonna go mingle.

339
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:19,360
So you work at Bloomingdale's, huh? My mom calls it "Bloomies."

340
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:26,280
Yeah, okay.

341
00:19:26,450 --> 00:19:28,040
At ease, soldier, heh.

342
00:19:29,830 --> 00:19:30,870
I'm sorry?

343
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:34,420
You can just drop the act. I know what's going on.

344
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:36,500
You're Danny's wingman, right?

345
00:19:36,670 --> 00:19:40,920
You guys are best buds, frat bros.

346
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:44,470
I'm going to go talk to, uh, a friend.

347
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:47,640
Yeah, you go talk to your friend.

348
00:19:47,810 --> 00:19:49,770
Go tell him, "Nice try."

349
00:19:53,730 --> 00:19:55,900
He just keeps lobbing them up...

350
00:19:56,110 --> 00:19:59,440
...and I keep knocking them right out of the park.

351
00:20:01,490 --> 00:20:02,610
I think I need a drink.

352
00:20:02,780 --> 00:20:04,280
Yeah.

353
00:20:08,450 --> 00:20:09,910
Ninety-eight...

354
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:11,620
...ninety-nine...

355
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:15,290
Okay. Go.

356
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:18,090
Dude, I'm telling you, I'm fine.

357
00:20:21,590 --> 00:20:23,340
Here we go, here we go.

358
00:20:24,090 --> 00:20:26,340
Hey.

359
00:20:24,090 --> 00:20:26,340
Hey.

360
00:20:26,510 --> 00:20:31,220
So I, uh, didn't get that apartment. Some problem with my application.

361
00:20:31,430 --> 00:20:32,600
You're kidding?

362
00:20:32,850 --> 00:20:36,980
But Phoebe said I could stay at her place for a while, so...

363
00:20:37,230 --> 00:20:40,690
Well, you can't stay with Phoebe. We're roomies.

364
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:43,690
You don't need me taking up all your space.

365
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:48,410
We got plenty of space. There's still some by that speaker.

366
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:51,120
Please, just stay.

367
00:20:51,290 --> 00:20:52,660
Yeah.

368
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:53,960
Are you sure?

369
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:57,250
Definitely.

370
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:57,250
You have to stay.

371
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:01,630
All right.

372
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:01,630
All right, buddy.

373
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:04,760
So I'm a pimp, huh?

374
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:09,260
It's okay.

375
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:11,760
Sometimes I can be a pain in the ass.

376
00:21:11,970 --> 00:21:15,690
But just talk to me. Tell me if something bothers you.

377
00:21:15,850 --> 00:21:22,230
And I'll do everything I can to keep my annoying habits just...

378
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:40,790
Well, I see you've had a very productive day.

379
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,250
The cowboy hat's a little much.

380
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:45,460
Come on, it's fun!

381
00:21:48,510 --> 00:21:49,550
All right.

382
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:58,270
Isn't this a woman's hat?

383
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:02,520
Dude, stop talking crazy, and make us some tea!

